  > 14 │       foo.firstName = "lorem";
       │       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    15 │       nested.inner.value = "lorem";
    16 │       return foo.firstName;
  
  i Vue decides when to run a computed property, and skips running it again while the values it reads stay the same. Changes made inside it happen at unpredictable times.
  
  i Make the change in a method or a watcher instead. To sort or reverse an array, work on a copy, as in [...items].reverse().
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

